Before talking about this blog, however, we must first go back to where it all began, when I started my FNF addiction
I remember it was around the release of FNF 0.6.0, which was basically a Pit Stop 2 update with new songs and new backgrounds
The exact date was probably a few days before, on March 29th, I believe
Fun Fact: I actually only believed the main game consisted of the regular levels for BF and Pico,
I did not learn about the Erect levels until I went into the files to listen to Roses Instrumental
(We’ll get back to this later, me “modifying” the game files is a trend throughout this year)
Anyways, I remember loving the idea of downloading games directly from itch.io since that was how I obtained FNF 
(*gasp* I know, I didn’t play on FNF until later)
FNF was my introduction to rhythm games, so at first, I was quite bad, having been new to the whole 4-arrow pressing schema
I would say now I can confidently beat all the current FNF levels at each difficult each time (except for Pico Nightmare, so tricky)

On May 15th, two days after all my exams had ended, I created this very blog to quench my frustration over no new FNF updates
Don’t get me wrong, I was used to waiting for new updates for Minecraft, but this felt more personal to me somehow
It was probably because of my insane obsession with anything to do with FNF at the time(except Newgrounds, we’ll come back to this)
Oh, those were the days, when I posted literally every day for 14 days
I remember those posts, I put quite a lot of effort on, because I had no idea how to write a blog
I’m way more proficient now, but before, I had to think deep in the recesses of mind for stuff to talk about
That’s why some of the earlier stuff (especially from May 15 to May 25) is based around older information
It’s only when I discovered the Funkin News and Funkin Remnants X account did I start incorporating their tweets in the mix

It, sadly, wasn’t all sunshine and rainbows, as I would learn
The first drama I was invested was not, in fact, Wandaboy, but the official itch.io comments
I had some beef with the people who were ragebating/lying about FNF, so I ranted about it on a post on May 26th
Even before the Wandaboy news, I was going through a really tough period in my life, and on May 28th, I proceeded to rant about digital presences online
The rant is now deleted as of June 16th, but if you saw it, again, I am so sorry for what I said, I’ll try not to let to it happen again
But anyways, after I said I was done with making FNF posts, I came back June 2nd to apologize and continue making these blog posts
And then came the Wandaboy drama and him getting banned of Newground (speaking of which, I hope he’s learning how to be a better person 
and not treating women like his playthings that can be disposed of)

It was during this period to early September that I was playing around with the game files and attempting the Erect levels
Turns out, it was quite easy to modify FNF, all I had to do was convert files from .mp3 to .ogg and rename to the original file name
If this sounds confusing, here’s an example for reference
One of the first files I modified, I believe, was girlfriends ringtone (which I had no idea existed until I went through the files)
I replaced the audio with Rick Astley’s “Never Gonna Give You Up” and put an apology txt file within FNF to ninjamuffin for modifying his game.
Also occurring this period was my insane playing of several FNF mods, starting with Midfight Masses
(man, Zavodilla is one of the best FNF mod songs ever)
Speaking of which, during July 9th to July 13th, I experimented with a series, but I decided to discontinue the idea, too much stress on me
It was also around this time that something of great importance was about to release

If I’m being honest, quite literally the only day I played FNF: The Mobile Port was when it releases
Quite ironic considering I had pre-saved since when it released on the App Store
I didn’t want to “torture” myself trying to learn how to use middle-scroll, and looking back, I kinda regret not doing it
But, at the same time, I know I would have raged so hard trying and also, you know how much battery life FNF drains away?
I play it for like 10 minutes and even on low power mode, it drains 6% of my battery
Knowing how long I play FNF on the PC, it definitely would not have been worth it to play FNF: TMP for more than an hour
I can only hope the optimization has been handled now, but anyways, now we move on to the greatest website of the [sic] world

To be frank, I discovered Newgrounds back in June, but I had only created an account during Mid-July.
I was watching all these amazing series that were amazingly popular, like the first I remember was, I think, ZTV News or PUNCH PUNCH FOREVER!
Looking back, I am grateful I created a Newgrounds account because there’s so much amazing content on there
Sure, there may be some flaws with the account creation/age setting verification and there are a LOT of NSFW artists on the platform
But overall, there are so many other creative talents too beyond just Madness Combat and the older series
I think one of the first “lesser-known” series I followed was Amber and Zoey’s web-show created by AWildDomino 
(which I highly recommend if you’re into wholesome content and life lessons)
I had only intended to create an account to browse the website and save some of my favourite submissions to the portal, 
5000 points later, I’m using the account to discover the newest talent and enjoy the amazing content that NG has to offer
Anyways, I’ve been talking about NG for a long time, if you wanna know more, read my July 26th post about it

